Some other things that generally may cause the kill counter of some
monster type get higher than the create counter:

- Bones files. When you encounter one of them, you get to kill monsters
that were not created in the current game, but in the one that left the
bones.

- Polymorph. When a polymorphed monster gets killed, the kill counter gets
increased for the monster class that it was killed as, but the create
counter was already increased for the original class.

- Monsters promoted. (kitten -> housecat -> large cat, little dog -> dog
-> large dog, soldier -> sergeant -> lieutenant -> captain, lich -> master
lich -> demilich -> arch-lich etc.) Counters work the same way as they do
for polymorphded monsters.

I don't remember how the counters are handled when you zap a wand of
undead turning at a corpse and I am too lazy to check now.

